  "modelled": {
   "vulva": "Modelled to textbook sizes on the HRA vaginal opening and pubic arch: clitoris (glans, body and crura along the ischiopubic rami), vestibular bulbs, greater vestibular glands, labia minora and majora.",
   "ovarian-vessels": "Modelled: neither body has the ovarian artery and vein; they run from the aorta (the left vein to the left renal vein, the right to the vena cava) down the back wall and through the suspensory ligament to the ovary.",
   "urethra": "Tubes on the path of the BodyParts3D urethra (too coarse to split), divided where it runs inside the prostate and the corpus spongiosum; widths after Gray’s Anatomy (prostatic about 6 mm, membranous 4 mm, spongy 5–6 mm with the navicular fossa).",
   "ejaculatory-duct": "Modelled tubes about 2 cm long from the end of each deferent duct, where the seminal vesicle duct joins it, through the prostate to the seminal colliculus.",
   "cavernosum": "The BodyParts3D corpora cavernosa (one mesh) cut into left and right at the midline septum; each deep (cavernosal) artery modelled along the middle of its corpus.",
   "endometrium": "Modelled lens in the plane where the HRA uterine walls meet: an inverted triangle about 3 cm wide at the fundus, from the internal os to about 9 mm below the fundus; thickness from about 1 mm (menses) to 14 mm (late luteal phase) as a morph target.",
   "gravid-uterus": "The HRA uterus wrapped by rays from its centre (an icosphere), with a morph target to a term uterus about 33 × 25 × 22 cm from the internal os to just below the xiphoid. The HRA full-term placenta set is placed on its inner posterior wall."
  }
